; DOMAIN: number-theory/cross-domain [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-24; provenance: David Navratil]
; Claim: The tribonacci constant eta (root of x^3=x^2+x+1, eta~1.8393; companion matrix T3 in SL(3,Z); cubic field Q(eta) disc=-44; Galois group S3) manifests structurally across ~24 distinct mathematical domains. These are structural convergences ("one root, many lenses"), not coincidences.
; Structure: 24-entry 3-root implication DAG. ROOT-subshift => (6 topological-entropy log(eta), 10 Arnoux-Rauzy IET p(n)=2n+1, 12 tribonacci-automatic sequences, 15 tribonacci morphic word, 16 tribonacci-synchronized DFA). ROOT-T3 => (4 T3 order 168 in GL(3,F13), 7 Rauzy fractal self-similar boundary, 11 B3 braid Yang-Baxter, 13 tribonacci numeration system, 14 3-regular compositions). ROOT-Pisot => (5 smallest degree-3 Pisot, 8 Parry number finite beta-expansion, 9 cubic field Q(eta) disc=-44, 17 continued fraction of eta, 18 3-type Galton-Watson, 19 LFSR coding theory, 20 JP algorithm terminates 8 steps). CROSS-ROOT bridges: (1 1D quasicrystal chain multifractal <= subshift+Pisot; 2 three-state Potts critical point <= Pisot; 3 phyllotaxis tribonacci spirals <= Pisot+dynamics; 21 Lindstrom enumeration <= automata+Pisot; 22 fan graph spanning trees <= numeration+combinatorics; 23 pseudo-Anosov dilatation genus 2 <= braid+entropy).
; Result: the 24 entries form a thesis(subshift)+antithesis(T3)+synthesis(Pisot) trialectical closure. 24 is a natural ceiling: beyond these 3 root objects, genuinely novel structural origins of eta are extremely rare (finite-generation bound from algebraic closure of the root triple). The bank itself instantiates the tribonacci pattern.
; Bridge: genesis_representation_theory (T3 order 168 in GL(3,F13), S3 Galois structure use character/representation tools) + genesis_perron_frobenius (eta is the Perron eigenvalue of the tribonacci companion/subshift transition matrix) + genesis_entropy_dynamics (topological entropy of tribonacci subshift = log(eta)).
